{
  "_comment": "Launches (SatelliteSimLaunches.cpp; plan .plans/LAUNCHES_PLAN.md). Each program keeps the constellations whose names contain one of its 'match' strings flying: every orbital plane is refreshed once per 'life_years', in launches of 'payload' satellites a 'batch_gap_days' apart. A launch flies from one of its vehicle's sites (one whose latitude and azimuth range reach the plane) at the moment the plane passes over it, deploys a train at 'park_km' that climbs to its slots over 'raise_days', and the satellites it replaces deorbit and re-enter over 'deorbit_days'. A program with a 'crew' block flies people to a station (a constellation of one) every 'life_years' (not scaled by the design-life setting): raise_days is lift-off to docking; no train, no retiree. Vehicle figures are public approximations (2036 is a guess). Sites: azimuth = [min, max] degrees clockwise from north, allowed by range safety (wraps through 360). Pads (drawn on the ground; sites within 150 m share one): optional 'pad_kind' (0 generic, 1 Falcon: service structure + landing zone, 2 Starship: catch tower; default from the vehicles flying there) and 'pad_heading_deg' (default the middle of the azimuth range). Vehicles: 'mount_m' = the launch mount the vehicle stands on, 'catch_m' = how far above it a tower-caught booster stops.",
